Canary pass -- which release versions the canary (husky) has smoke-tested, so the fleet may publish them (NWP-20261202-12).

Decisions of record: docs/product-decisions.md, 2026-10-30 ("every release is proved on a canary first -- husky joins
the release devices on a user build, publishes alone, and the rest of the fleet publishes only after its smoke test
passes"), and 2026-11-04 ("nine answers to harvest 57 -- every recommendation accepted", h57 #2), which gives the gate
its form: a committed canary-pass/<version>, read from the publishing checkout, or --without-canary, logged.

What reads it: `editions/endospore/build/canary-guard.sh <device> <version> [--without-canary]`.
`e4-ota-publish.sh` and `e4-ota-promote.sh` call it before any store write. The canary device (husky) publishes with
no file here. Any other device is refused for a version with no file here.

When husky's smoke test passes for a release, the operator writes a file named for the version (e.g. `0.5.55`) in the
publishing checkout, exactly three lines:

    canary husky
    build 2026120501
    smoke pass 2026-12-05

- `canary` names the canary device that ran the smoke test. It must be a device in the guard's CANARY_DEVICES.
- `build` is that device's build number, exactly 10 digits.
- `smoke pass` is the day the smoke test passed, as YYYY-MM-DD. No other word than `pass` is accepted.
- No fourth line, no blank line, no CR. A file that is not exactly this refuses, even with --without-canary (fail
  closed).

Then the operator publishes the fleet from the same checkout. The guard prints one line per device:
`canary-guard: <device> <version> follows canary husky build <BN>, smoke passed <date>`. The file is committed
afterwards, in the marker-bump PR that every release already gets (docs/release-runbook.md section 8).

`--without-canary` is the only bypass. Only Chester decides to use it. The guard then prints
`canary-guard: WITHOUT CANARY: <device> <version> is published with no canary pass (--without-canary)` on stderr;
quote that line in the release's worklog row.

Not guarded: the installer page publish (nowhere-cloud `publish-installer.sh`) does not read this directory. Publish a
fleet device's installer only after the pass file exists.

No pass file is committed with this README. Keep this README: the guard refuses when this directory is missing,
because its absence means a wrong checkout. Pinned by test-canary-guard.sh (--mutate).
